{"resourceIdentifier":"4525","resourceName":"The Republic of the Congo Improved Forest Management Project","description":"The Republic of the Congo Improved Forest Management Project (hereinafter referred to as “The project”) is located in UFA Djua-Ikié, The Republic of the Congo. It is implemented by Société d’Exploitation Foresrière Yuan Dong (hereinafter referred to as “SEFYD”) as the project proponent. The project is to protect the forest that was planned to be logged.\r\nUFA Djua-Ikié is located in the Souanké and Semé Districts of the Sangha administrative Province. The project is designed to improve forest management in 338,589 ha of native Congolese forests legally designated for logging. By avoiding previously planned logging and implementing improved forest management and conservation activities, this project will increase the carbon stock through protecting the forest.\r\nPrior to the implementation of the project, the forests in the project area were harvested following the guidelines in Timber Harvest Plan approved by the local forestry authority. In order to protect the forest ecosystem, improve the ecological environment, increase carbon sinks, reduce GHG emission reductions and slow down climate change, the project proponent decided to stop the logging and implement this improved forest management project activities from 01-August-2020 to 31-July-2040.\r\nThe project is expected to generate approximately 53,140,400 tCO2e during the 20 years’ crediting period, with the annual emission reductions of 2,657,020 tCO2e.\r\nThe project’s climate, community and biodiversity objectives:\r\n⚫ Reduce GHG emissions and mitigate climate change; and\r\n⚫ Improve soil and water conservation and contribute to sustainable development; and\r\n⚫ Provide experience of forest management and risk prevention and control for local stakeholders; and\r\n⚫ Improvement of the biodiversity and ecological environment of the project area and its surrounding area; and\r\n⚫ Increase employment opportunities and raise the income level of local residents; and\r\n⚫ Protect the local tree species from being cutting down.","location":{"latitude":1.551452,"longitude":13.335060},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-09-22","endExclusive":"2023-10-23","endInclusive":"2023-10-22"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4525"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Sangha Province"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Société d'Exploitation Forestière Yuan Dong"},{"type":"string","value":"Congo - Brazzaville, Congo"},{"type":"string","value":"+86-1366375479"},{"type":"string","value":"yuandong_congo@126.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Withdrawn"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2657020"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"IFM"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"VM0010"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"338589 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"CTI Certification Co., Ltd."}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 01/08/2020 - 31/07/2040"}]}]},{"programCode":"CCB","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Société d'Exploitation Forestière Yuan Dong"},{"type":"string","value":"Congo - Brazzaville, Congo"},{"type":"string","value":"+86-1366375479"},{"type":"string","value":"yuandong_congo@126.com"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Validation public comment period expired"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"2657